    "body": "## Motivation\r\n\r\nKDA graph tracking can read an FP32 chunk-boundary snapshot or a recurrent-state pool entry. With a BF16 state pool, these branches produce different Triton types, causing compilation to fail before the final store cast.\r\n\r\nObserved during GLM-5.3-Flash prefill BCG initialization with BF16 recurrent state:\r\n\r\n```text\r\ntriton.compiler.errors.CompilationError: at 19:4:\r\n    stride_h_row,\r\n    numel,\r\n    BLOCK: tl.constexpr,\r\n):\r\n    r = tl.program_id(0)\r\n    mode = tl.load(track_mode + r)\r\n    if mode == 0:\r\n        return\r\n    dst = tl.load(track_dst + r).to(tl.int64)\r\n    offs = tl.program_id(1) * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\r\n    mask = offs < numel\r\n    if mode == 1:\r\n    ^\r\nAssertionError(\"Mismatched type for val between then block (<['1024'], bf16>) and else block (<['1024'], fp32>)\")\r\n```\r\n\r\nA cast after the `if/else` cannot resolve this error: Triton requires matching types for `val` when merging the branches, before compiling the subsequent cast.\r\n\r\n## Modifications\r\n\r\nCast the snapshot to the state-pool element type before the branches merge. The stored dtype is unchanged, and FP32 state pools retain their existing behavior.\r\n\r\n## Accuracy Tests\r\n\r\nValidated in GLM-5.3-Flash PD serving on 8 × H200 with BF16 recurrent state and MTP516: GSM8K, 1,314 examples × 2 rounds, scored **95.4% / 95.9%**. These results are from the existing integration configuration containing this fix and the separate Decode RadixCache changes, not a new full-model run on this rebased PR branch.\r\n\r\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\r\n\r\n<!-- If this pull request impacts inference speed, provide benchmarking and profiling results. -->\r\n\r\nThis is a correctness fix; no inference speed improvement is claimed.\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\r\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\r\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\r\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\r\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\r\n\r\n## Review and Merge Process\r\n\r\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\r\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\r\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\r\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\r\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\r\n\r\n\r\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\r\n---\r\n### CI States\r\n\r\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39052843731](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39052843731)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39052843703](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39052843703)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\r\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:hourglass_flowing_sand: [Run #39052843832](https://github.com/sgl-projec